s junto al límite se reparten entre 81 adjudicatarios distintos. El contrato [1], de 39.546,83 euros, se adjudicó en diciembre de 2025.\nQué no pueden demostrar: El hecho de que se adjudiquen contratos al límite no indica que se hayan partido contratos ni que haya actuación maliciosa. Puede deberse a razones legítimas como precios de mercado o necesidades distintas.\nQué se puede revisar: Es necesario comprobar si los contratos [1] y [2] atienden la misma necesidad. También revisar si el adjudicatario A repite contratos en distintas áreas. Verificar si los contratos al límite se distribuyen según el tipo de obra.","en":"What the data shows: Between 2023 and 2025, this body awarded 103 minor contracts for works above 37,500 and up to 40,000 euros, just under the legal limit. If those amounts were spread as in the band immediately below, 9.0 contracts would be expected. The observed-to-expected ratio is 11.4, with a 95% confidence interval of 8.0 to 16.6. December accounts for 4% of the contracts just under the limit, compared with 7% of all its works contracts. The awardee with the most contracts just under the limit, called awardee A here, has 4. Contract [1], for 39,546.83 euros, was awarded in December 2025.\nWhat it cannot show: The high ratio shows a pattern, but it doesn't prove any wrongdoing. Prices might be low, budgets fixed, or needs separate. Statistical trends don't mean improper actions were taken.\nWhat can be checked: Check the December contracts for repeated purchases. Review awardee A's contracts to see if they cover multiple needs. Contract [1] could indicate a trend in late-year spending.","origen_es":"modelo","origen_en":"modelo","modelo":"Qwen3-4B (Q4_K_M, llama.cpp)","regla":"obras","citas":["%2FgOtBO6PxQDgL1BHd3qjQA%3D%3D","Nh6a2XGzdhq2gkLQ8TeYKA%3D%3D","zphATet2dqo%2Bk2oCbDosIw%3D%3D"],"generado":"2026-11-15"}}